1 ASSEMBLE

   Assembles VAX source into memory, from a file or, with no file, one
   statement at a time at the ASM> prompt.  The console takes it only
   until the microkernel is in place, which is how STARTUP.COM loads it
   (SYS$SOURCES:KERNEL.ASM on the system volume, or govax's built-in
   kernel.asm without one); after that ASM is a debugger command.
   ASSEMBLE is the same as ASM.

   Format

     ASSEMBLE [filespec]

   The file is a volume file or a host file, found as RUN finds one.
   HELP ASM at the DBG> prompt describes the assembler.
